# DESK29 -- a selection and a window change. Two windows on C:\ (the card has
# one partition, so the second window comes from double-clicking the same
# drive icon again: do_dopen calls win_alloc unconditionally,
# desksupp.c:1041-1063). Window 1 opens at (48,43), window 2 cascaded to
# (72,67), so window 1's work area is clickable at x < 72.
#
# Coordinates from the d-probe run:
#   C: drive icon                     click (38,35)
#   window 2, item 'README.TXT'       click (119,295)
#   window 1, empty work area         (60,300)  -- below its last item row
#                                     (obj 36 box (57,255) 76x40 ends at y 294)
200 parkbr
1000 arm
1100 mark A_IDLE
1500 move 38 35
1700 down
1703 up
1710 down
1713 up
2300 move 600 240
2900 mark B_WIN1
3200 move 38 35
3400 down
3403 up
3410 down
3413 up
4000 move 600 240
4600 mark C_WIN2
5000 move 119 295
5200 down
5203 up
5600 move 600 240
6200 mark D_SELECTED
6600 move 60 300
6800 down
6803 up
7200 move 600 240
7800 mark E_AFTER_TOP
# ...and window 2 back on top, so its (now empty) selection is visible again.
# Window 1 is 48..591 x 43..442, window 2 72..615 x 67..466, so window 2's
# horizontal scroll bar at y 448..466 is the uncovered strip: click (300,457).
8200 move 300 457
8400 down
8403 up
8800 move 600 240
9400 mark F_WIN2_BACK
